Why vendored rather than depended upon
    So that this repository stands alone. A judge, reviewer, or future
    maintainer can clone one repository and run the full demo, the tests, and
    the policy compiler with no other project present and no package index
    dependency. The three modules are stdlib-only by construction, so vendoring
    them adds no transitive dependencies.

Modifications made in this repository
    Four, all deliberate, all enumerated in the module docstring of
    `src/paypal_guard/governance/__init__.py`:

    1. `AuditTrail.verify_integrity` now recomputes each entry's hash and
       compares it to the recorded value, in addition to checking the chain
       links. Previously an in-place edit to an entry's payload was undetectable.

    2. `SafetyProtocol.decide_approval` no longer charges the session budget, and
       no longer records approvals through the monitor. Previously an approved
       action was charged and counted twice, once on approval and once on the
       retry that followed it.

    3. `SafetyProtocol.check_scope_only` is new, along with the read-only
       `frozen` and `revoked` properties. `execute` interleaves scope, budget
       and approval, so a caller could not ask the scope question on its own.
       A side-effect-free public scope check was added so that a caller can
       determine whether an action is in scope before performing priced work on
       its behalf. The guard needs this: it must know whether an action is in
       scope *before* firing an amount resolver, because that resolver is a live
       `orders.get`, and calling it for a merchant the agent was never granted is
       its own authorisation failure. Likewise, once the kill switch is engaged
       the guard must be able to observe that without calling `execute`, so it can
       skip the lookup entirely rather than issue PayPal reads during a fraud
       freeze. `frozen` and `revoked` expose those two conditions as plain
       properties. The method and the properties are pure.

    4. Unused `typing` imports removed and redundant `f`-string prefixes
       dropped, by `ruff check --fix`. No behaviour change. Style-only rules are
       excluded for this package, so that a later lint run cannot rewrite
       vendored code and silently widen the diff from upstream.

    No public API was removed or renamed. `frozen` and `revoked` are
    additions. No design or semantics were changed beyond the defect fixes
    above.

